&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Can Expect&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Interesting work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; - working in a fast-paced and ever-changing industry, new problems and exciting solutions are never too far away. There are always opportunities to learn new skills and broaden your horizons&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A sense of achievement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; - Our teams own their own software and when that awesome new feature ships to users and the positive feedback starts rolling in, you can feel really proud of what you and your team created&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Personal development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; - clear and defined career pathways for every role at every level, a supportive manager, loads of learning opportunities and even 10% of your time to dedicate to your learning.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Belonging&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt; - everyone at FanDuel works for each other, we win together, make mistakes together and have lots of fun doing it.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Trust - &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;A trusting work environment where productivity is valued above all else, giving you autonomy and ownership of your time and work&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Great financial package &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;- Including salary, bonus, pension, private healthcare, share save scheme, flexible working &amp;amp; holiday policy along with a number of other benefits.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;ABOUT FANDUEL&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FanDuel Group is the premier mobile gaming company in the United States and Canada. FanDuel Group consists of a portfolio of leading brands across mobile wagering including: America’s #1 Sportsbook, FanDuel Sportsbook; its leading iGaming platform, FanDuel Casino; the industry’s unquestioned leader in horse racing and advance-deposit wagering, FanDuel Racing; and its daily fantasy sports product. &amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition, FanDuel Group operates FanDuel TV, its broadly distributed linear cable television network and FanDuel TV+, its leading direct-to-consumer OTT platform. FanDuel Group has a presence across all 50 states, Canada, and Puerto Rico.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The company is based in New York with US offices in Los Angeles, Atlanta, and Jersey City, as well as global offices in Canada and Scotland. The company’s affiliates have offices worldwide, including in Ireland, Portugal, Romania, and Australia.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FanDuel Group is a subsidiary of Flutter Entertainment, the world&#39;s largest sports betting and gaming operator with a portfolio of globally recognized brands and traded on the New York Stock Exchange (NYSE: FLUT).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Diversity, Equity and Inclusion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;FanDuel is an equal opportunities employer. Diversity and inclusion in FanDuel means that we respect and value everyone as individuals. We don&#39;t tolerate bias, judgement or harassment. Our focus is on developing employees so that they reach their full potential.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;FanDuel is committed to providing reasonable accommodations for qualified individuals with disabilities. If you have a disability and need a workplace accommodation or adjustment during the application and hiring process, including support for the interview or onboarding process, please email&lt;span class=&quot;Apple-converted-space&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;ms-outlook-linkify&quot; href=&quot;mailto:Benefits@fanduel.com&quot;&gt;Benefits@fanduel.com&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The requirements listed in our job descriptions are guidelines, not hard and fast rules. You don’t have to satisfy every requirement or meet every qualification listed. If your skills are transferable and you are in the ballpark experience-wise, we&#39;d love to speak to you!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE POSITION&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Our roster has an opening with your name on it&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;FanDuel is hiring a Lead Product Manager to drive the strategy and execution of Account Management and Profile experiences across our portfolio of products — from Sportsbook and Casino to Racing, Daily Fantasy Sports, and new product categories on the horizon. From account creation and personal details management to profile customization and account settings, you&#39;ll shape how millions of customers manage their accounts and personal information across FanDuel every day, working at the intersection of customer experience, regulatory complexity, and multi-product ecosystem management.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll partner closely with Engineering, Product across other verticals, Risk/Fraud, Finance, Compliance, and Legal to build account management experiences that are customer-first, compliant, resilient, and built to scale. This is a high-impact role for an experienced product leader who wants to own meaningful&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to the specific responsibilities outlined above, employees may be required to perform other such duties as assigned by the Company. This ensures operational flexibility and allows the Company to meet evolving business needs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE GAME PLAN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everyone on our team has a part to play&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Strategy and Vision:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the Director of Product to define and communicate a clear product vision, strategy and roadmap for Account Management and Profile — balancing customer experience, operational efficiency, and regulatory/compliance requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Account Management Experience:&lt;/strong&gt; Own the end-to-end account management journey across FanDuel&#39;s portfolio — personal details, profile customization, account settings, and self-serve capabilities — designing experiences that balance ease-of-use with the controls, disclosures, and auditability required for a regulated environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Product Collaboration &amp;amp; Account Hub Evolution:&lt;/strong&gt; Enable seamless account experiences across all FanDuel products (Sportsbook, Casino, Racing, Predicts, DFS). Identify and drive self-service opportunities that reduce friction, increase customer autonomy, and improve the overall account management journey across the multi-product ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Industry and Product Expertise:&lt;/strong&gt; Build deep knowledge of account management product features, user journeys, and customer identity/profile best practices. Stay informed on market shifts, competitors, and emerging personalization technologies to refine the product roadmap.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Performance, Optimization &amp;amp; Metrics:&lt;/strong&gt; Drive measurable improvements in customer satisfaction, completion rates, and account feature adoption while maintaining strong controls. Establish, track, and communicate the success metrics (HEART scores, task success, conversion, user happiness) that matter and use a data-driven approach to prioritize work and demonstrate impact.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Self-Serve Expansion:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with Compliance, Legal, and Risk to evolve account self-service capabilities that increase customer autonomy while meeting regulatory requirements (e.g., customer verification, account settings management, T&amp;amp;C acceptance flows).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experimentation and Iteration:&lt;/strong&gt; Champion a test-and-learn approach: concept validation, A/B tests, pilots, and phased rollouts to validate account experience improvements before broad launches.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Product Quality and Delivery:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with engineering to ensure clear requirements, strong acceptance criteria, and high-quality launches. Manage dependencies, triage issues, and act as an escalation point to keep delivery on track across multiple product pods.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead complex initiatives end-to-end—from discovery and business case through delivery and iteration. Align stakeholders across Product, Engineering, Commercial, Finance, Legal, Compliance, Risk/Fraud, and Operations; remove blockers and drive decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Stakeholder Management and Influence:&lt;/strong&gt; Deliver concise, action-oriented communication and confidently present to senior leadership and cross-functional partners to secure buy-in, align priorities, and drive outcomes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE STATS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;What we&#39;re looking for in our next teammate&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;7+ years of product management experience with a track record of driving measurable business outcomes through customer-facing experiences.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with account management, identity, profile/personalization, or customer data products is preferred. We&#39;ll also strongly consider candidates with experience in adjacent domains — customer onboarding, conversion optimization, self-serve platforms, or marketplace account features.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ownership of complex, cross-functional initiatives with measurable business impact — e.g., user engagement, feature adoption, conversion, retention, revenue generation, cost optimization, or comparable KPI improvements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience leading and developing others as a direct manager — at least one product manager or analyst reporting to you, with evidence of their growth under your leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in regulated or compliance-sensitive environments, with experience partnering closely with Legal, Compliance, and Risk (or equivalent functions).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency: comfortable collaborating deeply with engineering on APIs, complex identity systems, multi-product architecture, and third-party vendor integrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong business acumen: crafting business cases, prioritizing tradeoffs, and communicating clearly with executive stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent written and verbal communication; able to influence without authority across senior leadership and cross-functional partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Passion for sports, sports betting, or sports-adjacent products; existing knowledge in these areas is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus: exposure to AI in a product context — whether that&#39;s using AI tools to accelerate your own product workflows, leveraging AI to build product features, or simply a strong curiosity and aptitude for incorporating AI into how modern PMs work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Don&#39;t check all the boxes? That&#39;s okay! We encourage you to still apply if you feel you possess adjacent skills and are interested in learning more.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p style=&quot;text-align: center;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
