&lt;p&gt;FanDuel is seeking a Manager, Tax Counsel to support FanDuel’s product and technology teams in tax product matters. This role sits at the intersection of tax, product, and engineering and will play a key role in ensuring tax requirements are effectively translated into and maintained across FanDuel’s customer-facing products.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will operate as a day-to-day advisor to cross-functional teams, translating complex federal, state, and jurisdiction-specific tax laws into clear, actionable guidance. You will partner closely with Product, Engineering, Tax, Legal, and Finance teams to support the ongoing integration of tax requirements into product functionality and user experience. Your guidance will directly inform product decisions and help shape how FanDuel delivers compliant, scalable customer experiences, while escalating complex or high-risk matters to senior tax leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In addition to the specific responsibilities outlined above, employees may be required to perform other such duties as assigned by the Company. This ensures operational flexibility and allows the Company to meet evolving business needs.&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;THE GAME PLAN&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Everyone on our team has a part to play&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide product-facing tax counsel to Product and Engineering teams across FanDuel platforms&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate federal, state, and jurisdiction-specific tax laws into actionable product and system requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interpret applicable tax statutes and regulatory guidance, including gaming taxes and customer tax reporting and withholding requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Review and advise on product features, enhancements, and existing product functionality to identify tax implications and compliance risks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor changes in tax laws, regulations, and industry standards, and advise stakeholders on relevant impacts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate cross-functionally with Tax, Legal, Finance Operations, Compliance, and Customer Support teams to ensure aligned execution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a key point of contact for tax-related product questions and cross-functional coordination&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Escalate complex, high-risk, or novel tax issues to senior tax leadership with clear analysis and recommendations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the development and documentation of tax positions and analyses related to product functionality, in partnership with senior tax leadership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support coordination with external stakeholders (e.g., regulators, vendors, and advisors) as needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist in ongoing product compliance monitoring and issue resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
