&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of shipping thoughtful, customer-centered products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong craft skills across interaction design, visual design, systems thinking, prototyping, and accessibility.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on fluency with modern design practices, design thinking, and evidence-based decision making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong analytical skills - comfortable using research, analytics, and feedback to inform and validate design decisions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional communication and collaboration skills; ability to influence without formal authority.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep customer empathy and a commitment to accessibility and inclusive design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A strong sense of ownership, a bias toward execution, and comfort operating in ambiguity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of experience in product design or a closely related role to start.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The scope you own, the strategic influence you carry, and the craft leadership we look for grow with the level you&#39;re hired into.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice to have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
